=== context initialization and clearing paths (proved) ===
INIT: ckt->CKTdiagctx = NULL UNCONDITIONALLY before every arm-condition
evaluation (niiter, before the intended CKTload) - it cannot be stale or
uninitialized on any unarmed iteration; the context itself is a stack-local
vtp_diag_ctx_t memset to 0 in the same iteration, valid through commit/discard.
ARM: vtp_armed==1 (target found) AND (iterno+1)==vtp_snap_iter AND time==0.0 AND
  MODETRANOP AND MODEINITFIX -> armed=1, CKTdiagctx=&vtp_ctx.
CAPTURE: target-instance-only (stamp_diag_active) pre/post reads into the ctx;
  writes touch ONLY the diagnostic-only context fields (permitted); no existing
  numerical matrix/RHS/state/model/device/node data is written.
CLEAR: every commit and every abort sets CKTdiagctx=NULL and armed=0; the
  unconditional NULL before the next arm evaluation is the second guarantee.

=== record-field contract (recount) ===
BEGIN  id tnode iterno time mode expected=3
col=100 id tnode iterno time mode col pre post delta
col=2   id tnode iterno time mode col pre post delta
RHS    id tnode iterno time mode pre post delta
END    id tnode iterno time mode emitted=3 expected=3
ABORT  id committed=0 tnode iterno time mode reason
  reason=load_error -> id=0 committed=0 (no dynamic id committed; never a stale or
  future id presented as accepted); reason=snapshot_failure -> the assigned
  vtp_snap_id with committed=0; reason=capture_missing|record_count_incomplete ->
  the assigned vtp_snap_id with committed=0 (missing existing entry -> records=0).
Successful family emits only after CKTload success AND SMPsnapshotMNA success,
carrying the actual dynamic id, tnode, authoritative iterno, time, mode; %a hex.

